From a9f6f442df37613ba977c5d2f7180e1250cf0f6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Hotchkiss <chris@hotchkiss.io>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:08:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] O3: oracle capture and control verbs over the P1 socket
 (GUAC_ORACLE=1)

Five verbs on P1's AF_UNIX listener so the oracle runs with nobody at the Mac (openspec AF.5, design decision 3). Each answers P1's ERR unknown_cmd unless GUAC_ORACLE=1 is in the emulator's environment, so a client that doesn't set it sees the product protocol. Nothing knows the game: every number is RSX's int_flip_index, the one STATE and HB already report.

- PAUSE_AT <flip> -> OK | ERR bad_flip | ERR no_renderer | ERR past. Pauses on that flip, where Start Paused pauses (rsx::thread::flip). The target is absolute and the RSX thread checks it at every guest flip, because a relative count set from the IPC thread races the RSX thread's decrement (the increment and the check sit a whole present apart). A target already passed is dropped and logged, never honored late.
- RESUME -> OK | ERR not_paused. Emu.Resume on the main thread, OK once it ran.
- RSXCAP -> OK | ERR busy | ERR no_renderer. Sets the flag the game window's capture shortcut sets; RSX arms at the next frame end, records the frame after it, writes captures/<TITLE>_<time>_capture.rrc.gz and pauses.
- SCREENSHOT -> OK flip=<n> | ERR busy | ERR no_renderer | ERR timeout. Sets the screenshot flag; VKGSRender::flip copies the guest's display buffer out of the surface cache at the next present and gs_frame::take_screenshot writes screenshots/<TITLE>/<TITLE>_screenshot_<time>.png. Paused, it asks for a native-UI flip (the pause message's path), which re-presents the current display buffer, so the shot is the frame the counter names. Replies once a present took the flag (5 s, then withdrawn).
- SAVESTATE -> OK | ERR not_running. The game window's savestate shortcut on the main thread: stop, write savestates/<TITLE>/*.SAVESTAT.zst, boot it again (Start Paused holds it 2 flips in). The client sends P5's RECONNECT after.

Touches Skylander.cpp beside P1 and three spots in RSXThread.cpp (the target, its reset with each RSX session, the check).

